#X text 240 83 mDNS (Multicast DNS) is a protocol that resolves host
names to IP addresses on a local network without a dedicated DNS server.
It operates over UDP port 5353 and uses the '.local.' domain suffix;
#X text 240 153 Service discovery in this object is based on DNS-SD
(DNS-Based Service Discovery) \, which uses standard DNS PTR \, SRV
and TXT records to advertise and find services;
#X text 240 208 Service '.local.' domain suffix is optional and can
be omitted;
#X text 240 248 There are service aliases: #osc - instead of '_osc._udp.local'
\, #http - '_http._tcp.local' \, #all - to subscribe to all available
services on the network;
#X text 240 303 Note: on close the object will automatically unregister
any previously registered services;
#X text 240 343 Note: the #all service is a special case — it outputs
all available network service names with the format [service SERVICE(;
